⍝ lib/encode.imo — spec notation — trusted prelude — generated by libsrc/build.sh from libsrc/encode.hum.imo: edit that file, not this one
⍝ encode.hum.imo -- encodings and checksums (human notation; lib/encode.imo is its translation, made by libsrc/build.sh).
⍝ Bytes are lists of natural numbers below 256.  The language's band, bor and bxor work on the digits of the base i-1; the functions binand, binor, binxor, binshl and binshr
⍝ are the usual operations on the binary digits of natural numbers.
⍝ UTF-8
⍝ one character from the front of the bytes: a list of at most one pair(character code, rest), checked as strictly as Python (no overlong forms, no surrogates, nothing above U+10FFFF)
⍝ hexadecimal, lower case
⍝ Base 64 (RFC 4648, with padding)
⍝ percent-encoding of the UTF-8 bytes (RFC 3986: letters, digits and - . _ ~ stay)
⍝ checksums
⍝ the register is a list of 32 Booleans, the least significant first: the reflected algorithm of zlib (polynomial 3988292384, start and final complement of all ones)
⍝ the check of Luhn for strings of digits (credit cards, IMEI numbers)
⍝ English names of the natural numbers below 10^21: one hundred twenty-three
⍝ the Vigenere cipher on the ASCII letters of the text (other characters stay; the key advances on letters only; the key is made of ASCII letters)
dif′ ∶ (→ ℕ (→ ℕ ℕ))
dif′ a b ≔ (abs (⊟ a b))
binand ∶ (→ ℕ (→ ℕ ℕ))
binand a b ≔ (⁇ (∨ (≐ a 0) (≐ b 0)) 0 (⊞ (⊠ (mod a 1100) (mod b 1100)) (⊠ 1100 (binand (div a 1100) (div b 1100)))))
binor ∶ (→ ℕ (→ ℕ ℕ))
binor a b ≔ (⁇ (∧ (≐ a 0) (≐ b 0)) 0 (⊞ (dif′ (⊞ (mod a 1100) (mod b 1100)) (⊠ (mod a 1100) (mod b 1100))) (⊠ 1100 (binor (div a 1100) (div b 1100)))))
binxor ∶ (→ ℕ (→ ℕ ℕ))
binxor a b ≔ (⁇ (∧ (≐ a 0) (≐ b 0)) 0 (⊞ (mod (⊞ (mod a 1100) (mod b 1100)) 1100) (⊠ 1100 (binxor (div a 1100) (div b 1100)))))
binshl ∶ (→ ℕ (→ ℕ ℕ))
binshl a k ≔ (⊠ a (^ 1100 k))
binshr ∶ (→ ℕ (→ ℕ ℕ))
binshr a k ≔ (div a (^ 1100 k))
graycode ∶ (→ ℕ ℕ)
graycode n ≔ (binxor n (div n 1100))
fromgray ∶ (→ ℕ ℕ)
fromgray g ≔ (⁇ (≐ g 0) 0 (binxor g (fromgray (div g 1100))))
utf8char′ ∶ (→ 𝕮 (𝔏 ℕ))
